+# Implementation Plan — Parent Attendance Access
 
 ## Goal
-Bring the pages outside the dashboard (Attendance, Timetable, Materials, Homework, Marks) up
-to the same header/spacing consistency established in the dashboard passes, one page at a time.
+Fix the flagged bug where parents fell through to the teacher marking view on the Attendance
+page, and give them a real read-only view — following the same ParentStudentLink-resolved
+scoping pattern already used by Homework and Materials.
 
-## This session: Attendance page only
-- Swap both `TeacherAttendanceView` and `StudentAttendanceView`'s manual eyebrow+`<h1>` header
-  markup for the shared `DashboardHeader` component, matching the dashboard's header style
-  and spacing exactly.
-- No other structural changes — the page's tab system, marking grid, and stat displays were
-  already well-built and visually consistent with the pine/saffron/paper system; only the
-  header needed unifying.
+## Changes
 
-## Explicitly not touched this session
-- The `AttendancePage` role switch only branches on `role === 'student'` — parents currently
-  fall through to the teacher marking view. This is a functional bug tied to the deferred
-  `ParentStudentLink` work, not a styling issue, so it's left alone here to avoid conflating
-  UI polish with the pending backend/access-control fix.
-- Timetable, Materials, Homework, Marks pages — queued for subsequent sessions.
+1. **`src/app/api/attendance/route.ts`**
+   - `requireRole` now includes `'parent'`.
+   - Resolve a parent's linked children (`ParentStudentLink` → `childIds`) and their batches
+     (`linkedBatchIds`), then scope the BatchSubjectTeacher filter to those batches — same
+     shape as the existing student/teacher branches.
+   - Records now include `student: { select: { name: true } }` so a parent with multiple
+     children can tell rows apart (the frontend `AttendanceRecord` type already had an
+     optional `student.name` field anticipating this).
+   - New `hideRecordsExceptChildren` helper (parent equivalent of the existing
+     `hideOthersRecords` for students) — filters each session's `records` down to just the
+     parent's own children, and sets `myRecord` when exactly one child appears in a session.
